cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "A Neuro-Symbolic Framework for Automated EU AI Act Article 9 Compliance Verification"
authors:
  - family-names: "Vahedi Sarrigani"
    given-names: "Hoda"
    affiliation: "Liverpool John Moores University"
abstract: >-
  A three-layer neuro-symbolic framework for automated verification of EU AI Act
  Article 9 (risk management) compliance for healthcare AI systems. Layer 1
  extracts the regulation into a SHACL-validated knowledge graph and checks
  structural completeness; Layer 2 uses an LLM to verify semantic coherence of
  the mitigation hierarchy and risk severity; Layer 3 is a dual-shield graph
  neural network classifying compliance under evidence noise, with confidence-
  based escalation to human review. Evaluated on a synthetic dataset grounded in
  ISO 14971 and public FDA submissions.
keywords:
  - "EU AI Act"
  - "compliance verification"
  - "neuro-symbolic AI"
  - "knowledge graphs"
  - "graph neural networks"
  - "SHACL"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-01"
